# List page and pagination standard

New list/table/grid screens must consume the shared kit. Do not copy page-size arrays, paginator markup, or view-toggle buttons into a module.

## Pagination

- Use `<app-paginator>` under the content. Summary on the **left**, page size + Previous/pages/Next on the **right**.
- Grid and table share one size: **10**. Options: **10, 20, 50, 100** from `UI_PAGINATION`.
- Import sizes from `src/app/shared/config/ui-standards.ts`. Never hard-code `pageSize = 20` on a page.
- Parse API pages with `normalizePagedResult()` so both Spring `number` and `PageResponse.page` work.
- Query params: `page` (0-based), `size`, `sort`.

## Toolbar

Use `<app-list-toolbar>` whenever the page is a real searchable list (students, staff, users, roles, catalogs). Skip it only for tiny datasets (e.g. a handful of sections).

Fixed structure, left to right:

1. Search (~4/12)
2. One to three page-specific filters
3. **Search** and **Reset**, immediately beside those controls
4. Grid / Table icons, far right — not in the filter cluster

Placeholders, filters, and tooltips may differ. The layout must not.

## Search vs filters (backend pagination)

- **Text search** is live with debounce (`UI_SEARCH.debounceMs`). Bind `(searchDebounced)` to query. It queries the **backend** for the full dataset, then the API paginates. Never filter only the rows on the current page.
- **Dropdown/date filters** stay in the form until the user clicks **Search** (or presses Enter). Keep a committed copy of those filters; debounce search must reuse the last committed filters, not the unsubmitted dropdown values.
- Bind `(submitted)` to copy draft filters → committed, then query. Do not fire an API call on every dropdown change.
- **Reset** clears search, filters, optional sort, and page (back to 0), cancels a pending debounce, and reloads the default query.
- A new search/filter resets the **page number** only. Keep view mode, page size, and the typed/selected form values.

## Partial refresh

Do not wrap the whole page in `*ngIf="!loading"` for search/filter. Keep header, stats, toolbar, and view toggle mounted. Use `<app-list-results [busy]="refreshing">` so only the table/grid shows a loading overlay. First visit may skeleton the results area; later queries overlay the existing rows.

Grid and table are the same query. Only the template changes.

## Grid / table view

- Use `<app-grid-table-toggle>` (already included by `app-list-toolbar`). Icons: grid (`pi-th-large`) then table (`pi-list`).
- The parent initializes `view` from `ViewPreferenceService.globalDefault()` (or `initialView(saved.view)` after Back).
- The toggle is presentational: bind `[mode]` and handle `(modeChange)`. Do not resolve preference inside the toggle. Do not persist the page switch as a global setting.
- Persist list pagination/search/view with `ListContextService` before navigating to detail/edit so Back restores context. A fresh visit from the menu uses the global default again.

## Cards

Use the shared `.app-data-grid` density (`minmax(280px)` auto-fill). Cards must `min-width: 0` and wrap/ellipsis so content never overlaps or spills past the card width.

## Back navigation

- Deeper pages (detail, edit, create, wizards) use `<app-back-nav [fallback]="'/app/.../list'">` or `BackNavigationService`.
- Do not leave users with only the side menu as a way back.

## Modal vs dedicated page

- **Modal**: few fields, quick add/edit, little surrounding context (e.g. Add Category).
- **Dedicated page**: many fields, tabs/sections, or a major workflow (admission, student, staff, customer, organization).

## PrimeNG tables

If a screen still uses `p-table` paging, set `[rows]="10"`, `[rowsPerPageOptions]="[10, 20, 50, 100]"`, `[showCurrentPageReport]="true"`, and `currentPageReportTemplate="Showing {first}–{last} of {totalRecords} results"`.
